        <div class="docs-sidebar-inner">

            <div class="docs-nav-title">
                DOCUMENTATION
            </div>

            <nav>

                <a href="#overview" class="docs-nav-link active">
                    Overview
                </a>

                <a href="#getting-started" class="docs-nav-link">
                    Getting Started
                </a>

                <div class="docs-nav-group">
                    <div class="docs-nav-heading">
                        SDK
                    </div>

                    <a href="#sdk-overview" class="docs-nav-link">
                        Overview
                    </a>

                    <a href="#installation" class="docs-nav-link">
                        Installation
                    </a>

                    <a href="#core-concepts" class="docs-nav-link">
                        Core Concepts
                    </a>

                    <a href="#blocks" class="docs-nav-link">
                        Blocks
                    </a>

                    <a href="#worlds" class="docs-nav-link">
                        Worlds
                    </a>

                    <a href="#modding" class="docs-nav-link">
                        Modding
                    </a>
                </div>

                <div class="docs-nav-group">
                    <div class="docs-nav-heading">
                        REFERENCE
                    </div>

                    <a href="#api" class="docs-nav-link">
                        API Reference
                    </a>
                </div>

            </nav>

        </div>

    </aside>


    <!-- Main -->
    <main class="docs-main">

        <div class="docs-content">

            <!-- Header -->
            <div class="docs-breadcrumb">
                Documentation
                <i class="bi bi-chevron-right"></i>
                Overview
            </div>

            <h1 id="overview">
                Crafty Documentation
            </h1>

            <p class="docs-lead">
                Documentation for the Crafty platform, engine, and developer SDK.
            </p>


            <!-- Disclaimer -->
            <div class="docs-warning">

                <div class="docs-warning-icon">
                    <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <strong>Early Development</strong>

                    <p>
                        The Crafty SDK is currently in early development.
                        APIs, namespaces, interfaces, and behaviors may change
                        rapidly between releases. Documentation may occasionally
                        lag behind the latest implementation.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>


            <!-- Getting Started -->
            <section id="getting-started" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    GETTING STARTED
                </div>

                <h2>
                    Start building with Crafty
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Crafty provides a developer-focused platform for creating
                    mods, extensions, and custom content. The SDK exposes the
                    systems required to interact with the Crafty runtime.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Because the SDK is still evolving, this documentation
                    focuses on the APIs and workflows currently available.
                </p>

                <div class="docs-next-grid">

                    <a href="#installation" class="docs-card">
                        <div class="docs-card-icon">
                            <i class="bi bi-download"></i>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <h3>Installation</h3>
                            <p>
                                Set up the Crafty SDK in your development environment.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <i class="bi bi-arrow-right docs-card-arrow"></i>
                    </a>

                    <a href="#sdk-overview" class="docs-card">
                        <div class="docs-card-icon">
                            <i class="bi bi-box"></i>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <h3>SDK Overview</h3>
                            <p>
                                Learn how the Crafty SDK is structured.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <i class="bi bi-arrow-right docs-card-arrow"></i>
                    </a>

                </div>

            </section>


            <!-- SDK -->
            <section id="sdk-overview" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    SDK
                </div>

                <h2>
                    Crafty SDK
                </h2>

                <p>
                    The Crafty SDK provides the APIs and tooling required
                    to build extensions and mods for Crafty.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The SDK is designed to expose the functionality developers
                    need without requiring direct access to the internal
                    implementation of the engine.
                </p>

                <div class="docs-code">

                    <div class="docs-code-header">
                        <span></span>
                        <span></span>
                        <span></span>

                        <label>C#</label>
                    </div>

                    <pre><code><span class="keyword">using</span> Crafty.SDK;

<span class="keyword">public sealed class</span> ExampleMod : IMod
{
    <span class="keyword">public void</span> Initialize()
    {
        <span class="comment">// Your mod starts here.</span>
    }
}</code></pre>

                </div>

            </section>


            <!-- Installation -->
            <section id="installation" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    SDK
                </div>

                <h2>
                    Installation
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Install the Crafty SDK through the distribution method
                    provided for the current release.
                </p>

                <div class="docs-code">

                    <div class="docs-code-header">
                        <span></span>
                        <span></span>
                        <span></span>

                        <label>Terminal</label>
                    </div>

                    <pre><code>dotnet add package Crafty.SDK</code></pre>

                </div>

            </section>


            <!-- Core Concepts -->
            <section id="core-concepts" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    SDK
                </div>

                <h2>
                    Core Concepts
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Crafty exposes several core concepts that form the
                    foundation of the SDK.
                </p>

                <div class="concept-list">

                    <div>
                        <strong>Worlds</strong>
                        <span>
                            Persistent voxel environments managed by Crafty.
                        </span>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Blocks</strong>
                        <span>
                            The fundamental building units of a voxel world.
                        </span>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Mods</strong>
                        <span>
                            Extensions that add or modify functionality.
                        </span>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <strong>Resources</strong>
                        <span>
                            Assets and data consumed by the platform.
                        </span>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </section>


            <!-- Blocks -->
            <section id="blocks" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    SDK
                </div>

                <h2>
                    Blocks
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Blocks represent the individual elements that make up
                    Crafty's voxel worlds.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Block registration, models, textures, and behavior are
                    exposed through the SDK as the relevant systems mature.
                </p>

            </section>


            <!-- Worlds -->
            <section id="worlds" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    SDK
                </div>

                <h2>
                    Worlds
                </h2>

                <p>
                    World APIs provide access to the voxel environment and
                    the systems responsible for managing world data.
                </p>

            </section>


            <!-- Modding -->
            <section id="modding" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    MODDING
                </div>

                <h2>
                    Modding
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Crafty is designed with modding as a first-class feature.
                    The SDK provides the foundation for developers to extend
                    the platform without modifying the core engine.
                </p>

            </section>


            <!-- API -->
            <section id="api" class="docs-section">

                <div class="docs-eyebrow">
                    REFERENCE
                </div>

                <h2>
                    API Reference
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Detailed API reference documentation will expand alongside
                    the Crafty SDK as its public surface stabilizes.
                </p>

            </section>

        </div>


        <!-- Right TOC -->
        <aside class="docs-toc">

            <div class="docs-toc-title">
                ON THIS PAGE
            </div>

            <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
            <a href="#getting-started">Getting Started</a>
            <a href="#sdk-overview">SDK</a>
            <a href="#installation">Installation</a>
            <a href="#core-concepts">Core Concepts</a>
            <a href="#blocks">Blocks</a>
            <a href="#worlds">Worlds</a>
            <a href="#modding">Modding</a>
            <a href="#api">API Reference</a>

        </aside>

    </main>

</div>


